      "flags": true,
      "name": "BUTTON",
      "source": {
        "column": 5,
        "file": "flags.cpp",
        "line": 43
      },
      "usage": [
        "Bit flags: each value is one bit (`BUTTON.JUMP` is `1 << 0`) or a union of bits, so combine values with `|` and",
        "test them with `&`. The `*_mask` functions take these values; `test_mask` is true when any of the given bits is set.",
        "The `*_flag` functions take a bit number counted from 1 instead (`BUTTON.JUMP` is bit 1). All of them return the",
        "new number and leave their argument unchanged.",
        "",
        "```lua",
        "local flags = set_mask(0, BUTTON.JUMP | BUTTON.WHIP) -- both on",
        "flags = clr_mask(flags, BUTTON.WHIP) -- BUTTON.WHIP off",
        "flags = flip_mask(flags, BUTTON.WHIP) -- BUTTON.WHIP on again",
        "if test_mask(flags, BUTTON.JUMP) then",
        "    flags = clr_flag(flags, 1) -- BUTTON.JUMP off, by bit number",
        "end",
        "flags = set_flag(flags, 1) -- BUTTON.JUMP on",
        "flags = flip_flag(flags, 1) -- BUTTON.JUMP off",
        "```"
      ],
